{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786605701639,"sessionID":"ses_0060d0225ffe6aY2TL9kC9SIMN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_ET_B39GfHZCVlP6ByTixLkd6498","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Whether to adopt the optional z_archive/ sub-split for genuinely-complete leaf phases in addition to the 9-grandparent grouping\",\n    \"Whether 057-phase-consolidation-research should be renamed/absorbed into the implementation packet once the proposal is approved\",\n    \"Whether the migration should be one commit or one commit per grandparent group (M7 options)\"\n  ],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    \"Q1: Merging/grouping the 036 children into fewer multi-phase parents is feasible and beneficial — spec-kit health check classifies 45 children as error and recommends splitting into nested phase parents (iter 1)\",\n    \"Q2: 9 grandparents cover all 45 children, program-ordered and dependency-safe (iter 2-3)\",\n    \"Q3: M0-M7 migration plan with lockstep surface updates, hash recompute, regeneration of specs/descriptions.json, gates, and lossless rollback (iter 4)\",\n    \"Q4: timeline.md schema — seq=created_at, stable_id=slug, moved_to, append-only renumber ledger (iter 5)\",\n    \"Q5: Risks = validate.sh hash-lock, pre-existing 053-056/057 drift, symlink, regenerated index; gates = M6 + timeline verification (iter 4-5)\"\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    \"45 on-disk children (001-033, 035, 047-057); 13 already phase-parents holding 61 grandchildren; 32 leaves\",\n    \"is-phase-parent.js health returns error (45 > 40 threshold): 'Split into nested phase parents'\",\n    \"validate.sh hardcodes a 40-entry sha256-locked 036 manifest (001-033, 035, 047-052); 053-056 are on disk but absent (pre-existing drift)\",\n    \"specs/descriptions.json is a regenerated MCP folder-discovery cache (3207 entries, 133 036-related) — never hand-edit\",\n    \"050-trustworthy-state-records.created_at = 2026-07-27 (before 019-032) but numbered 050 — numeric prefix is not chronological\",\n    \"034<->036 renumber precedent (commit 8d3b5b21d57) + specs-root flip (606e55cb8a9) make raw git first-commit dates unusable per-child\",\n    \"9-grandparent grouping drops 036 direct children 45 -> 10, all groups <= 11 members (healthy)\"\n  ],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n    { \"approach\": \"45-child manifest is acceptable\", \"reason\": \"Tooling classifies as error; recommends nested phase parents\", \"evidence\": \"is-phase-parent.ts:125-145\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"Numbering scheme B (tail-band reuse)\", \"reason\": \"Reads arbitrarily, fights taxonomy\", \"evidence\": \"iter 3\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"Rewriting historical research/lineage logs\", \"reason\": \"Append-only evidence\", \"evidence\": \"rg inventory\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"Hand-editing specs/descriptions.json\", \"reason\": \"Regenerated MCP cache\", \"evidence\": \"folder-discovery.ts:1236-1330\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"validate.sh manifest update without sha256 recompute\", \"reason\": \"Hash-lock breaks validation\", \"evidence\": \"validate.sh:217-246\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"Numeric prefix as timeline sort key\", \"reason\": \"050 anomaly refutes it\", \"evidence\": \"created_at data\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"Raw git first-commit as timeline sort key\", \"reason\": \"Specs-root flip made dates uniform\", \"evidence\": \"git log\" },\n    { \"approach\": \"Mutable timeline.md\", \"reason\": \"Would destroy chronology guarantee\", \"evidence\": \"iter 5 design\" }\n  ]\n}\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-b/findings-registry.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop